  <model metaid="meta_talinolol_kidney" id="talinolol_kidney" name="Model for talinolol elimination in the kidneys" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Model for talinolol elimination in the kidneys</h1>
        <p>Model for the renal excretion of talinolol (tal)
encoded in <a href="http://sbml.org">SBML</a> format.</p>
        <p>Talinolol is excreted unchanged in the urine by glomerular filtration and
a net tubular secretion: the renal clearance (151-311 ml/min) is several
times the filtration of the unbound talinolol. The renal excretion is the
filtration of the unbound talinolol <code>GFR * fup_tal</code> times <code>TALEX_f</code> (1 is
filtration alone, above 1 a net secretion), so that it follows the renal
function as the glomerular filtration rate does.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>On average, about 60% of talinolol and talinolol metabolites was excreted by kidney and about 40% extrarenally.
{Trausch1995}</li>
          <li>Other metabolites then talinolol are almost not detectable in urine. I.e. sum of metabolites is 0.33% of dose
vs. talinolol 52.83 % dose {Trausch1995}</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
