    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_renal_function" name="renal function" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <blockquote>
              <p>1.0: increased kidney function
1.0: normal kidney function (healthy control)
&lt;1.0: decreased kidney function</p>
            </blockquote>
            <p>Renal function relative to the healthy glomerular filtration rate
GFR_base, which is 101 ml/min at 75 kg; a measured creatinine
clearance of X ml/min is the renal function X/101.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="GFR_base" name="glomerular filtration rate (healthy)" value="101" units="ml_per_min" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="fup_tal" name="fraction unbound in plasma tal" value="0.4" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="TALEX_f" name="renal clearance of unbound talinolol relative to the GFR" value="7.66469242599538" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The renal clearance of talinolol is TALEX_f times the filtration of
its unbound fraction, fup_tal * GFR: 1 is filtration alone, above 1 a
net tubular secretion. A renal clearance of 151-311 ml/min
(Westphal2000a/b, Trausch1995, Schwarz2007) is TALEX_f 3.7-7.7 at
fup_tal 0.4 and GFR 101 ml/min.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
